{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes","id":1195352,"title":"Mega-Attributes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T10:07:45-07:00","id":1195352,"title":"Mega-Attributes","content":"So i heard that they are removing Mega-Attributes from the Aberrant system. So I was wondering if this is a term thing or a full it's gone thing. Additionally does this mean Enhancements are going as well. <br /> <br /> Because honestly why I don't mind the pure dot level or term of Mega-Attribute goes I hope Enhancements as buyable powers stay. I loved those things. Still do actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ps. I didn't kickstart the new Scion so I don't have access o the documents that might answer how they did it there with Epic Attributes. <br /> <br /> PPS. I hope someday they bring back Atlantis in Scion as I for one loved that. Hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:45:50-07:00","id":1195372,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, nothing in Aberrant is written in stone yet. Or on paper. Like, development is just begining, if it's even started.<br /> <br /> Either way, Core and \u00c6on have nothing about Mega-Atts because those aren't things that Talents or Psions get.<br /> <br /> I'm personally hoping they're in and they work to increase your scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:42:19-07:00","id":1195477,"title":"","content":"Remember that the concept of Scale originated in <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b> as part of its superheroes hack: if it <i>doesn't</i> get used in a similar way in <b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b>, I'll be sorely disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:20:08-07:00","id":1195496,"title":"","content":"As for Enhancements: <br /> <br /> 1. The core Storypath system already has a specific use for the term \u201cEnhancement\u201d; so at the very least, the name is going to have to change.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm not sure I want <b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b>'s equivalent of the original Enhancements to use the Attributes as an organizing principle. I'd rather go with something similar to the new <b>Scion</b>'s Callings, mechanically: conceptually, call them something like \u201cAugmentations\u201d and group them into conceptually similar types which sometimes parallel the Attributes and other times don't. For instance, Augmentation categories might be: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> \u2022 Strength (1e's Mega-Strength Enhancements)<br /> \u2022 Mobility (1e's Mega-Dexterity Enhancements)<br /> \u2022 Fortitude (1e's Mega-Stamina Enhancements)<br /> \u2022 Form (1e's Mega-Appearance Enhancements and the Body Modification Quantum Power)<br /> \u2022 Senses (1e's Mega-Perception Enhancements)<br /> \u2022 Genius (1e's Mega-Intelligence and Mega-Wits Enhancements)<br /> \u2022 Charm (1e's Mega-Charisma and Mega-Manipulation Enhancements)<br /> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:30:51-07:00","id":1195500,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar509_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"509\" data-vbnamecard=\"509\">TiwazTyrsfist</a> What has me asking is that the writers have mentioned removing both mega attributes and epic attributes. So while the books haven't been written yet, and so things can change, it was somewhat noted. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <br /> <br /> I looked up the Mage Chronicles Guide scale rule again. Interesting and a nice way to go. I also like the whole note about there being better ways to sjow power then by giving more dice to roll. <br /> <br /> On 1, good point and Augmentation is a good word as well. Gives the right feel too, as Quantum energies augment the human norm. <br /> <br /> On 2, I can see how that would work and make sense. Even more it separates desogn space from having to link 1 for 1 with attributes. For example I knew of many people who created a Mega-Willpower category, which in this system would work more easily. <br /> <br /> I can definetly see the benefits of doing it thus way. Plus it keeps the individual category powers, which is basically what I wanted. <br /> <br /> As a note I wish I could read the Callings of Scion 2. Do you know of any posted for display purposes as I didn't kickstart it .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:35:09-07:00","id":1195506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1195500#post1195500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note I wish I could read the Callings of Scion 2. Do you know of any posted for display purposes as I didn't kickstart it .</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wont copy and paste them, I can give a summary if you'd like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:38:34-07:00","id":1195507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1195506#post1195506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I wont copy and paste them, I can give a summary if you'd like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if your willing as that would help mightily. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:47:20-07:00","id":1195510,"title":"","content":"Creator: Both in the Progenitor, and Creative aspects<br /> Guardian: Protectors of People, Places or Things<br /> Healer: Healers of Body, Mind, and Soul<br /> Hunter: Pursuer, and Perceptive Stalkers<br /> Judge: Lawgivers and Punishers of the &quot;Wicked&quot;, how ever they chose to define it.<br /> Leader: Rulers and Inspirational Figures<br /> Lover: Both Romantic, and Platonic love, the best friends, and lovers<br /> Liminal: Outsiders, and those that journey<br /> Sage: Scholars, Teachers, and 1/2 of the Clever<br /> Trickster: The other 1/2 of the Clever, and those who flout the rules and get away with it<br /> Warrior: Kind of self explanatory, but just in case: See big thing, kill big thing, survive big things counter attack when hitting it the first time didn't work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Obviously the actual descriptions are far less tongue in cheek, and have a lot more depth and flexibility, but these basic descriptions should give you a rudimentary understanding of what types of things fall under their sway.<br /> <br /> **Also, you get 1 Calling at Origin, which must come from one of your Divine Parents 3 Callings. When you reach Hero, you choose 2 more Callings, which may be any you desire, regardless of your Parents 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 03-14-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:52:50-07:00","id":1195513,"title":"","content":"Note that I suggested changing Body Modification from a Quantum Power to the Augmentations; it's a much more natural fit there, though it wouldn't have worked with the Mega-Attributes setup. It also makes it easy to draw parallels between Augmentations and Aberrations: both are kinds of Alterations to the Nova's body and mind, the difference being that Augmentations would be largely beneficial while Aberrations are largely detrimental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:54:41-07:00","id":1195514,"title":"","content":"Oh cool. Thanks for that. (Also your descriptions are fun.)<br /> <br /> And each Calling has a set of powers to purchase or gain? <br /> <br /> That's actually a really nifty and intriguing system. <br /> <br /> I mean I'm pretty sure I'm buying Scion when it comes out, lol. But it's nifty to see things that make me go &quot;ooh shiny, that sounds fun!&quot;<br /> <br /> @Dataweaver<br /> <br /> I saw the move of body modification and i like that quite a lot. It feels better as an Augmentation than a straight up power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:01:17-07:00","id":1195517,"title":"","content":"Each Calling provides a set of Knacks that let you do things, similar to Ab1e's Enhancements or Ad1e's Knacks. <br /> <br /> For Aberrant 2e, I'd be sure to have the Strength Augmentations include one that increases your effective Scale for the purposes of lifting, breaking, and throwing large objects. Similarly with other things in the game that Scale applies to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-14-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:05:27-07:00","id":1195519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1195514#post1195514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh cool. Thanks for that. (Also your descriptions are fun.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1195514#post1195514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And each Calling has a set of powers to purchase or gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each calling has a Rating from 1-5. Origin Characters have 1 Calling at Rating 1. Hero Characters have 4 or 5 points (depending on which part of the preview you are currently reading) distributed between their 3 Callings. With a minimum of 1 in each calling. You get 1 free &quot;Knack&quot; (What the powers are called) from each Calling for every Rating it has. Ratings cannot be purchased, but instead raise naturally thru the increasing of your legend. You may purchase Knacks with XP, but can have no more &quot;active&quot; per Calling then it's Rating. You can switch out which Knacks are active each game session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1195514#post1195514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a really nifty and intriguing system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is. I like it a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:47:28-07:00","id":1195526,"title":"","content":"Not a bad system, not at all. I could totally see them going with something like that, as Novas are quite powerful beings in ways similar scion characters. <br /> <br /> That said, if they do go woth it I hope they don't put a limit on active knack-equivalents or prohibit the buying of new levels in the categories.<br /> <br /> But the idea of categories having dot ratings themselves while also having there own knack-like makes perfect sense for the set up of Aberrant. <br /> <br /> And let's be honest some of the Scion 1e design space came from what Aberrant had done. So it's fair for them to share. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Gah. All this makes me want Aberrant all the more. I did they choose to do it first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T03:03:30-07:00","id":1198280,"title":"","content":"So how high do Mega Attributes go? Like do Tier three Nova's have God level strength? How does Enhanced mental attributes vary by Tier? What does it look like for 2nd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T03:32:39-07:00","id":1198285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198280#post1198280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how high do Mega Attributes go? Like do Tier three Nova's have God level strength? How does Enhanced mental attributes vary by Tier? What does it look like for 2nd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t look like anything yet, as they\u2019re nowhere near being written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T08:32:55-07:00","id":1198330,"title":"","content":"Mega Attributes created a lot of the flavor for Aberrant 1E, but at the same time there were balance issues with them that never quite got resolved - even after errata. So if they do return, they'll need some revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:03:57-07:00","id":1198337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198330#post1198330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mega Attributes created a lot of the flavor for Aberrant 1E, but at the same time there were balance issues with them that never quite got resolved - even after errata. So if they do return, they'll need some revision.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we won't know for absolute certain until <b>TC: Aberrant</b> comes out, we <i>have</i> been told that the reason why the Storypath System included Scale was to serve as a replacement for the Epic/Mega-Attribute mechanics from the original gamelines. That's why I said that I'll be sorely disappointed if <b>TC: Aberrant</b> <i>doesn't</i> go that route. <br /> <br /> And I don't want to see Mega-Attributes return, as flavorful as they were, because I don't want 1e's Enhancements to be straitjacketed by the Attribute grid. Do something more like <b>Adventure!</b>'s Dynamic Knacks (which are similar to <b>Aberrant</b>'s Enhancements), and replace Mega-Attributes with \u201cDynamic Knacks\u201d that increase Scale appropriately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T09:47:30-07:00","id":1198345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198337#post1198337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> we <i>have</i> been told that the reason why the Storypath System included Scale was to serve as a replacement for the Epic/Mega-Attribute mechanics from the original gamelines. That's why I said that I'll be sorely disappointed if <b>TC: Aberrant</b> <i>doesn't</i> go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also be highly disappointed if Mega-Attributes returned in TC:Aberrant. The Storypath Scale makes it seem at least <i>somewhat</i> feasible to eventually have a campaign that features a Psion, a Nova and a Scion existing alongside each other with relative parity. If suddenly the Nova has access to a level of powers that far outstrips the other two it would instantly kill any hope of such a crossover. As much as I love the existing Aberrant materials, I like the idea of a Continuum timeline that can serve as a sort of Silver Age Superhero world - some of the character concepts someone would want to play in that would be better served by a Scion than a Nova and at first blush it seems Storypath allows for that without much major hacking at the system.<br /> <br /> I've also never really been a fan of just how broken Mega-Strength is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T10:29:37-07:00","id":1198356,"title":"","content":"For me it's the 'enhancements' I like the most, with a dash of being so super powered my character could punch a car into orbit. The term mega-attribute never called to me as an in setting thing, I did like it's ability to pump up the scale of things. <br /> <br /> That said, I do admit to not caring about balance between the groups. I want my Novas to be powerful figures capable of world shattering events while Psions are individually no match but collectively can do great things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T11:24:39-07:00","id":1198367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me it's the 'enhancements' I like the most, with a dash of being so super powered my character could punch a car into orbit. </div> </div> </div>While being that strong is fun, it can be challenging as an ST to create balanced encounters for a group that has one player with Mega-Strength who can deal enough damage to take out any normal human with a single hit. So if it were to return I'd be concerned with how it balances against other Novas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I do admit to not caring about balance between the groups. I want my Novas to be powerful figures capable of world shattering events while Psions are individually no match but collectively can do great things. </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily care about direct correlational balance between Psions and Nova's, but I don't want Storypath to become the system where there are wildly disparate sub-systems from one game to the next. Scion, TC and TC: Aeon may be skinned a little differently - but at their core they do at this point seem to be the same basic system without too much wild deviation. <br /> <br /> I'm also not sure I like the idea of Novas getting an in-system ability to go beyond the normal attributes and do amazing world shattering things, while the children of the gods over in Scion aren't capable of the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T11:35:21-07:00","id":1198370,"title":"","content":"Who says that they aren't? Thus far, we've only seen <b>Scion: Hero</b>. For all we know, demigods will be quite capable of up-Scaled feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T12:10:52-07:00","id":1198374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198370#post1198370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that they aren't? Thus far, we've only seen <b>Scion: Hero</b>. For all we know, demigods will be quite capable of up-Scaled feats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that Demigod will scale up what they can do, but I don't imagine it will do so through the introduction of Mega-Attributes. I'm saying that the inclusion of Mega-Attributes in Aberrant would give a starting Nova a significant power advantage over a starting Scion - since we know that Mega-Attributes don't exist in Scion: Hero. <br /> <br /> As an example: with a version of Mega-Attributes you could through XP with one core book build a Nova and raise him to a power level approaching Superman, while with the core book that we currently are aware of for Scion you could not build a Scion and raise him to a power level approaching Thor.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:49:02-07:00","id":1198432,"title":"","content":"That's because the Scion books we currently have are <b>Origin</b> (which is Tier 1) and <b>Hero</b> (which is Tier 2), whereas the Trinity books both feature Tier 2 types (Talents and Psions). Novas are Tier 3, and we're not going to be getting the Tier 3 Scion book until <b>Demigod</b> comes out. If we get to that book and still don't have a way of Scaling Might into the range of comic-book Thor<sup>\u2605</sup>, <i>then</i> I'll be worried. But for now, I don't see any problem.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> \u2605 I specify \u201ccomic-book Thor\u201d because <b>Scion</b>'s Thor is a full-on Tier 4 <i>god</i>, more akin to Galactus or the Beyonder than to the \u201cpuny god\u201d that Hulk smash. \u201cComic-book Thor\u201d is a demigod in <b>Scion</b> terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:59:57-07:00","id":1198439,"title":"","content":"The thing that frustrates me is that I'm not use t i didn't kickstart Scion, though I know in the future I will buy it. <br /> <br /> What frustrates me is I really want to see the rules variances it has as compared to Trinity - like the divineish powers of Hero and the way that gods are written up. <br /> <br /> That frustrates me because I assume certain elements of how the gods of Scion are written up will be used as inspiration for elements of Aberrant. <br /> <br /> Which leads me to asking, does anyone know of any example powers posted by the devs of Scion for free read through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:49:15-07:00","id":1198458,"title":"","content":"It feels insanely appropriate for a Nova that can uproot a skyscraper to be able to one shot a human. It would be weird if they couldn't in fact... Everyone doesn't need to be balanced in that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:27:51-07:00","id":1198507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198458#post1198458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels insanely appropriate for a Nova that can uproot a skyscraper to be able to one shot a human. It would be weird if they couldn't in fact... Everyone doesn't need to be balanced in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Mega-Strength\u2019s automatic damage a character with MS 5 can one shot more than just a standard human because he delivers 25 automatic lethal not counting attack successes.<br /> <br /> I get that you feel that this is appropriate from a tonal perspective, but this is still a game where the player who can one shot a human could also conceivably one shot other PC\u2019s just as easily - it SHOULD be balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:31:50-07:00","id":1198508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198507#post1198507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Mega-Strength\u2019s automatic damage a character with MS 5 can one shot more than just a standard human because he delivers 25 automatic lethal not counting attack successes.<br /> <br /> I get that you feel that this is appropriate from a tonal perspective, but this is still a game where the player who can one shot a human could also conceivably one shot other PC\u2019s just as easily - it SHOULD be balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I not saying we should use the same system bro. Scion 1st ed was even more wacked out and you could do much more then 25 automatic lethal. I think the system will not be the same.<br /> <br /> But I do feel super strong beings of high tier should be able to punch a man's skull off and into the nearby countryside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:36:53-07:00","id":1198513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198508#post1198508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do feel super strong beings of high tier should be able to punch a man's skull off and into the nearby countryside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... okay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:40:04-07:00","id":1198515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198513#post1198513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh... okay</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the games have the potential to combo powers that would be super deadly to starting class and competitive to high class. Vampires can combine Potence, Celerity, and Protean, along with unique powers to boost knockback. Werewolves can boost strength with gifts, turn your fists into silver and amplify damage. Mages can boost forces.<br /> <br /> Its not like it would be easy but High level novas should be something you need numbers to take out or another high tier character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:59:57-07:00","id":1198542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires can combine Potence, Celerity, and Protean, along with unique powers to boost knockback. Werewolves can boost strength with gifts, turn your fists into silver and amplify damage. Mages can boost forces. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Vampires can combine multiple Disciplines into a unique and stronger power to deal more damage. So can Werewolves, so can Mages. Mega-Strength 5, with its own enhancement of Crush (which you can get free when you buy your first dot of Mega-Strength) delivers 25 automatic successes to an attack roll in the form of lethal damage. It is not combined with any other power to do this. You are describing oranges to tell me why the apple tastes the way it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Its not like it would be easy but High level novas should be something you need numbers to take out or another high tier character. </div> </div> </div>A high level physical nova in 1st edition already is something you need another high level nova to contend with, but a high level mental or social nova will die at the hands of the high level physical nova quite fast and squishilly because the old system wasn't balanced.<br /> <br /> And with certain Quantum Powers you didn't even have spend all the XP it took to get to Mega-Strength 5 because powers like Sizemorph gave you levels in it FOR FREE. I once ran a game where a starting character was able to buy sufficient sizemorph to have MS 5 and upended the first session of the game by killing 2 PC's each with one hit. <br /> <br /> That's the kind of stuff I'm talking about when I say it was broken, and that the new version of the game needs to be balanced.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:39:18-07:00","id":1198564,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is you don't need 25 auto successes to represent someone punching someones head off and into the clouds. And in this edition you can use other attributes for defense. They are more free flow with the rules and what skill + Atts are needed.<br /> <br /> But its almost like super powered humans can do things others can't do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:50:51-07:00","id":1198567,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind the way Scale works: it either multiplies the effectiveness of what you're doing, or it gives you additional Enhancements to work with. It depends on how significant to the plot the subject of your action is. Per the Scale rules, Superman can easily pick up a skyscraper and toss it around; but if he attempts to punch Luthor in the face, he is <i>not</i> guaranteed to send Luthor's head flying. Not because it wouldn't be \u201crealistic\u201d; but because Luthor is too important to die that easily. <br /> <br /> This allows you to have your cake and eat it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:55:17-07:00","id":1198568,"title":"","content":"Well exactly. I don't mind so much that the punch towards Luther won't kill him, but that after fighting the punch that full on connects and ends the fight, I want that to be his head flying into the clouds.<br /> <br /> We don't need the 25+ auto successes, Scion got even worse with that, and it became inconsequential outside of physical combat because nobody else could have 50+auto successes to compete with Epic Manipulation or Intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T06:40:59-07:00","id":1199023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1198345#post1198345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've also never really been a fan of just how broken Mega-Strength is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In play, I was perpetually surprised at how massively damage outpaced defensive powers (and not just for Mega-Strength, quantum bolts chewed through force fields pretty darn fast, too!). It was just a super-deadly game.<br /> <br /> I had a character with armor *and* mega-stamina, and it seemed like any time she got punched by someone with mega-strength, it was a near-death experience. (OTOH, she also had Mega-Strength and Claws, for cheap lethal attacks, and if she hit someone, they were pretty much dead, too, so it was like hand-to-hand-range-rocket-tag...)<br /> <br /> Mega-strength and Mega-stamina, IMO, should have been at least closer to balanced. Even cutting Mega-strength down to three auto-successes per dot (or five extra rolled dice, instead of auto-successes?) might have been a good start.<br /> <br /> Still, I loved the power level of Aberrant. I'd hate to see it reduced too much, to balance a '30 Nova point' Nova to team with an Adventure-style Daredevil or Stalwart, or a Trinity-era Psion. IMO, the solution there, in a crossover style game with a Daredevil, a Psion and a Nova, would be to give the Nova fewer Nova points, somewhere between 5 and 15, depending on what you are going for (and perhaps to give the Adventurer! and Psion more of their own resource points; more Psi, more 'Facets,' more dots for Modes / points for Knacks, etc.).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:48:43-07:00","id":1199155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199023#post1199023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I loved the power level of Aberrant. I'd hate to see it reduced too much, to balance a '30 Nova point' Nova to team with an Adventure-style Daredevil or Stalwart, or a Trinity-era Psion. IMO, the solution there, in a crossover style game with a Daredevil, a Psion and a Nova, would be to give the Nova fewer Nova points, somewhere between 5 and 15, depending on what you are going for (and perhaps to give the Adventurer! and Psion more of their own resource points; more Psi, more 'Facets,' more dots for Modes / points for Knacks, etc.).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My first concern is making sure that Novas balance against each other. You\u2019re right in that a nova with claws can be just as deadly as a nova with mega-strength. But for balance there is no reason that either of those should be able to one hit kill a telepath who focused on all mentals. <br /> <br /> The Scale system in Storypath goes a long way to making tier play scalable in a fair and balanced way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T13:12:01-07:00","id":1199161,"title":"","content":"But the thing is not all powers are combat powers... Telepathy and Mega Intellect has great use out of combat so its kind of natural for it to not be the be all and end all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:31:28-07:00","id":1199193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199161#post1199161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is not all powers are combat powers... Telepathy and Mega Intellect has great use out of combat so its kind of natural for it to not be the be all and end all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the penalty for building a non combat character in the system is to be instantly killable by the combat character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:40:34-07:00","id":1199201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199193#post1199193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the penalty for building a non combat character in the system is to be instantly killable by the combat character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you know don't get in a fist fight with a guy who can uproot redwoods... All gamelines were like this even Exalted, there is a major difference between pure combat builds and light combat builds. This is a game based on teamwork so if you are squishy rely on help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:59:02-07:00","id":1199206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199201#post1199201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you know don't get in a fist fight with a guy who can uproot redwoods... All gamelines were like this even Exalted, there is a major difference between pure combat builds and light combat builds. This is a game based on teamwork so if you are squishy rely on help.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Exalted was not like this, there was no power stat that with less than 100 XP expended you were granted a dice bonus that eliminated any potential defense by giving you a 25 dice bonus to your attack without the use of combining charms. <br /> <br /> You keep talking about other game lines and the way you combine powers... Mega-Strength is a single game breaking power - and Mega Atts aren\u2019t even the primary \u201cpower group\u201d in the game.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t believe it\u2019s broken? Try this experiment, pull out the book and build an NPC with the best possible defense allowable in the game. Then throw a 5 strength, 3 brawl, 5 Mega Strength attack against it. <br /> <br /> How many rounds does it hold up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:21:23-07:00","id":1199218,"title":"","content":"Dude I already admitted it was broken first thing, it will have a new system, and the 25 auto successes was a mess in Scion so its a mess here. And that is not how Exalted Works...25 dice pools are not particularly unique with 100 exp to spend... Besides 3rd Ed Exalted is a different beast, as will be 2nd ed Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:36:41-07:00","id":1199224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199218#post1199218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude I already admitted it was broken first thing, it will have a new system, and the 25 auto successes was a mess in Scion so its a mess here. And that is not how Exalted Works...25 dice pools are not particularly unique with 100 exp to spend... Besides 3rd Ed Exalted is a different beast, as will be 2nd ed Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Explain in Exalted 1e how you can get a 25 dice pool to a punch roll to hit WITHOUT using a charm after spending 100 xp or less. With max strength, max brawl, a specialization in brawl we\u2019re at 13 dice. It\u2019s going to cost a lot more than 100 xp to buy the essence necessary to raise the cap on the strength to get the extra 12 dice to get us to 25 dice.<br /> <br /> To get those kind of dice on a to hit you actually have to use a charm - most times a combo of charms. Scion also requires abilities to get to that level of dice. Neither game could get you there at creation - but through the sizemorph loophole you CAN get there in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> 2. Mega Strength doesn\u2019t give you a 25 dice pool, it gives you 25 dice to add to your dice pool. There\u2019s a slight difference.<br /> <br /> 3. If you agree that it\u2019s broken then what in the sweet hell is the point of coming back post after post to defend it by suggesting that it\u2019s \u201cinsanely appropriate?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:56:30-07:00","id":1199233,"title":"","content":"I'm saying super strength is appropriate, and I have confidence that 2nd ed will fix it.<br /> <br /> And why would you not let the Exalted use charms, Mega-attributes would be a charm in Exalted... That's like saying okay now how the Nova use a perfect defense to block an N/A damage meteor... without super powers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:09:17-07:00","id":1199241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199224#post1199224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Mega Strength doesn\u2019t give you a 25 dice pool, it gives you 25 dice to add to your dice pool. There\u2019s a slight difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking 1e Aberrant Mega-Strength? If so, this is incorrect. Mega-Strength 5 gave you an automatic 25 *successes* to your roll, but didn\u2019t add anything to your dice pool. (Unlike other Mega Attributes, which did add to the pool.)<br /> <br /> It was very broken. I hope 2e Aberrant keeps something like Mega Attributes, but scale and Enhancement are better ways of it working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:21:13-07:00","id":1199244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199233#post1199233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying super strength is appropriate, and I have confidence that 2nd ed will fix it.<br /> <br /> And why would you not let the Exalted use charms, Mega-attributes would be a charm in Exalted... That's like saying okay now how the Nova use a perfect defense to block an N/A damage meteor... without super powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I disallow charms in the example?<br /> <br /> 1. Because Meg-Attributes are not the corrollary to charms - Quantum Powers are. Mega Attributes are cheaper and easier to purchase than charms and QP.<br /> <br /> 2. To illustrate further that your constant bringing up of Exalted is an apples to oranges comparison. You keep saying that you can do the same things in Exalted that you can do in Aberrant, and flat out: no, you can\u2019t. You need to spend more xp to get to those kind of pools and you have to expend essence to use the charms to do it. MA\u2019s are cheap and cost nothing to use. I.E. not the same. Also, Exalted has higher level defenses that hold up better against high powered attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:26:06-07:00","id":1199246,"title":"","content":"But in Exalted all super powers are charms, except for spells and evocations which are essentially like charms anyways but squinted. The cost of charms differ only if you favor them.<br /> <br /> I don't know where this is going. Everyone already agreed early editions are rather Hax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:37:18-07:00","id":1199251,"title":"","content":"I think that these two statements are not opposites. <br /> <br /> 1) A nova focused on punching should be set to punch something into orbit. <br /> <br /> 2) A nova should not immediately loose because he chooses to face a nova who likes to punch things to orbit. <br /> <br /> Part of the problem in 1e is that they used the WOD system which is about monsters with powers in he might not super powered beings like Superman or Magneto. So the rules didn't always match the setting. <br /> <br /> Which for me is a no brainer, let the setting win. <br /> <br /> It's also why I don't mind i f Mega-Attribute as a term disappears. People in setting didn't say &quot;I'm Mega-Strong&quot; for all that we could see them doing certain things that fit the concept. It's basically why I said &quot;hey even if they change the name are the enhancements of 1e still going to be there&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T17:26:27-07:00","id":1199261,"title":"","content":"Meh. Mega strength is a little too good early game, I guess. Late game it\u2019s basically useless though. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d say the problem doesn\u2019t lie with mega strength. It lies with mega stamina, and the really weird soak powers. Force field is really good. Armor is not. Mega stam is only useful in powering force field. Etc.<br /> <br /> And it all explodes once you put mastery on quantum bolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T19:39:53-07:00","id":1199281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199261#post1199261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say the problem doesn\u2019t lie with mega strength. It lies with mega stamina, and the really weird soak powers. Force field is really good. Armor is not. Mega stam is only useful in powering force field. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lies with both. Part of Mega-Strength\u2019s problem was that it didn\u2019t follow the same rules as other Mega-Attributes, which resulted in it not playing nicely with others.<br /> <br /> This is part of why Scale could work well - you can compare and work out effects accordingly. If Nova A has Mega-Strength giving +2 Scale and Nova B has Mega-Stamina giving +2 Scale, they cancel each other out and you roll normal dice pools for both. If Nova A attacks a Baseline, that poor sap is going to whomped. etc. Nova A also has the edge against Novas with Mega-Stamina giving only +1 Scale, and will struggle against those with +3 Scale. For example.<br /> <br /> You also have to remember that none of this can be considered in isolation. Storypath is a different system - damage doesn\u2019t work the same way, Defence doesn\u2019t work the same way. You can\u2019t just \u2018fix Mega-Strength\u2019 without taking into account how Mega-Strength interacts with the rest of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T19:42:29-07:00","id":1199283,"title":"","content":"Why is the mega strength 5 guy even attempting to hit the mega charisma guy? Convince him you are best friends. It will be cake, since he burned all his nova points getting quantum 5 and mega strength. Or dominate him into killing himself. Or poison him, unless he also bought mega stam. In which case, steal his quantum energy or steal HIS mega strength and kill him with it.<br /> <br /> Also, Invulnerability is 6 auto soak to basing and lethal per dot. Kinetic is an acceptable form to take without adding an extra. Punching is kinetic damage. So Invulnerability is stronger, point for point, than Mega Strength...AND Inv counts towards aggy damage of the matching type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T07:51:38-07:00","id":1199369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1195352-mega-attributes?p=1199251#post1199251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that these two statements are not opposites. <br /> <br /> 1) A nova focused on punching should be set to punch something into orbit. <br /> <br /> 2) A nova should not immediately loose because he chooses to face a nova who likes to punch things to orbit. </div> </div> </div> </div>1.) I don\u2019t think anyone has an issue with the concept of mega strength getting to the level where you can indeed punch something into space, the issue is that this is a role playing game and the progression to that power is almost non-existent. If, like in games like Exalted, it took multiple powers combined or a lengthy XP sink to get from lifting a truck to killing a normal guy by flicking his nose I don\u2019t think anyone would have much to complain about.<br /> <br /> 2.) This speaks to the issue as addressed earlier in the thread - this is still a game system so there needs to be parity of level progression. Near perfect \u201cto hits\u201d need a near perfect defense to counter it. Otherwise one power dominates the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}